> During the ospi_read_sfdp, no command complete IT occurs, the ospi remains busy (bit 5 of the OCTOSPI_SR).

I think I know what the issue is because I struggled with the same thing. The current HAL driver `HAL_OSPI_Command_IT` does not support sending/receiving data. I had to change my driver to rather use `HAL_OSPI_Command`. It's caused by there's the following line in `stm32h7xx_hal_ospi.c:983`:
```
if (... && (cmd->DataMode == HAL_OSPI_DATA_NONE) && ..){
    // Do command
}
else
{
    status = HAL_ERROR;
    hospi->ErrorCode = HAL_OSPI_ERROR_INVALID_SEQUENCE;
}
```

If you read the `hospi->ErrorCode` you should see it set to `HAL_OSPI_ERROR_INVALID_SEQUENCE`.

